{
 "title": "Vertex paint: colour attributes",
 "summary": "Vertex paint on a Suzanne subdivided (level 3, applied) so it has vertices to paint: Dirty Vertex Colors with Normalize off darkens the crevices, stored in the colour attribute and shown through an Attribute node's Fac in the base colour. Then painting parts: an Eyes attribute (white) with red eyes and nose, a Head attribute with a green crown, each read by an Attribute node into colour B of a Mix Color, light blue for the rest, the factors 0.5. Beyond the tutorial: a toadstool in one mesh and one material -- the cap painted red through the face selection mask, white spots dabbed with the brush, grime from dirty vertex colours in a second attribute multiplied in.",
 "objects": [
  {
   "name": "DirtMonkey",
   "description": "dirty vertex colours"
  },
  {
   "name": "PaintedMonkey",
   "description": "painted eyes, nose and head"
  },
  {
   "name": "Toadstool",
   "description": "vertex-painted toadstool"
  }
 ],
 "expected_result": "A grimy grey Suzanne, a pale blue Suzanne with pink eyes and nose and a green crown, and a red toadstool with white spots on a cream stem.",
